    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nRecently I started using `mini.files`,  I'm using lazy.nvim as my package manager.\r\n```\r\n{ 'echasnovski/mini.files', version = '*' }\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt works fine, but at every nvim startup I'm getting this error\r\n```\r\nError detected while processing BufEnter Autocommands for \"*\":\r\nError executing lua callback: ...n.m/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1154: scoped variable: Invalid buffer id: 1\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function '__index'\r\n        ...n.m/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1154: in function <...n.m/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1150>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tried using the latest branch by setting `version = false`, still same issue. I even tried mini.nvim, still same issue\r\n\r\n        \r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nI followed the steps specified in https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.files\r\n1. In lazy.nvim  add this dependency `  { 'echasnovski/mini.files', version = '*'}`\r\n2. call require('mini.files').setup() in lua\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nShouldn't throw any error at startup\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThrowing error at startup",
